A||N||5||CoolBlue87GT||A letter to Pontiac's Historical division||||6||
Z||000000||CoolBlue87GT||06-17-2001||01:17 AM||||I found a site that is for Pontiac's Historical division.<P>This is part of a letter I sent off to them today.  Thought you all might enjoy.<P><BR>To :  Pontiac Historical Division<P>I've been told to contact the Pontiac Historical web site about my 1987 Pontiac Fiero GT.<P>My Pontiac Dealer has given information about your site, and he is very proud of the<BR>Fiero's also. <BR> <BR>The Fiero, as you know, has a had, and has a huge following.<BR> <BR>The last two car shows I went to had over 120 Fiero's. We are very proud of the Fiero, and intend to never let them die. <BR> <BR>We hope it will earn it's rightful place in Pontiac's History as one of the Best Sports cars ever designed by Pontiac and produced.<BR> <BR>We all are of course, saddened that the decision to stop production was made.  We know now, the assumption that the 2 seater sports cars were not wanted by the public was<BR>a little off.<BR> <BR>Seeing with interduction of the Mazda Miata, Toyota MR2,  Porsche boxter, and now BMW<BR>are enjoying success, the public is still hot for 2 seaters.<BR> <BR>I can only hope those that made those decisions are now retired and not making anymore fatal errors.<BR> <BR>The Saturn's of course, owe there existence using the technology from the Fiero.  <BR>  - but that's another story.<BR> <BR>I hope this and any other letters from fellow Fiero owners will help, is I said before, earn it's rightful place in Pontiac's History as one of the Best Sports cars ever designed by Pontiac and produced.<BR> <BR>As for mine, I'm the original owner, bought new in 86.   As of July 16 2001, it has only<BR>1760 miles !! It is 100% Factory stock and has been well accepted at the shows.<BR> <BR>Thousands of Fiero owners have been enjoying and showing their's much longer than me.<BR>One web site that deserves a link from your site is Pennock Fiero Forum. Many enjoy this<BR>site to exchange information, and enjoy each others Fiero's.<P>Our prayer, Please bring the Fiero back !<BR> <BR>Thank you for providing the space and taking the time to read this.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000001||JetroGT||06-17-2001||05:37 AM||||That's a great letter. I hope Pontiac thinks so too. I usually get negatives when I talk about my Fiero at the dealer ship. And they always sigh when they see me come in for service.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/JetroGTsig.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000002||johnt671||06-17-2001||09:17 AM||||The Pontiac dealer in Hazleton told me he had no one qualified to work on mine.  Two months later he was out of business.  Wonder what other Pontiacs they weren't able to fix.||||reg||1
Z||000003||CoolBlue87GT||06-17-2001||10:31 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by johnt671:<BR><B>The Pontiac dealer in Hazleton told me he had no one qualified to work on mine.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Luckly my best friend has his own shop. <P>A few years ago I had trouble with my front brakes.  I went to pull it out for a nice drive, and the front wheels were locked and would not turn !<P>The dealer over the phone was telling me the it was going to be about $400 dollars to fix.<P>I had the car towed to my friends shop, and turns out the piston had locked up (see pic)in both the brakes.  Moisture had form rust, and the piston could not retract.<P>With part & labor, his bill was 53 dollars. While he was at it, he rebulit both calipers.<BR>Was funny is, the parts came from that same Pontiac dealer.  (this was in Md, have a much better dealer here in Fl, this owner loves Fieros)<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1del1.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||6
Z||000004||firstfiero||06-17-2001||02:29 PM||||      A  mechanic at the shop I use worked on fieros at pontiac dealer in the 80s. He loves working on my fiero and is glad to see it when it comes in. I have a suspicion that he joy rides a little after he's done working on it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> anyway he laughes when I tell him this and can't understand why their so hard to work on!<P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif">         <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||GT-maniac||06-18-2001||08:42 PM||||The letter sounds good, hopefully they'll at least take it seriously. I've been to my local Pontiac dealer so often they now know me by name and give me a discount. Of course that's what happens when your working on two fieros at the same time..||||reg||1
